# Git commits

Follow [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/#summary) for every commit message.

## Format

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

- **Subject**: lowercase type, optional scope in parentheses, colon + space, then a short imperative summary (no period).
- **Body** (optional): blank line after subject; explain *why*, not a file list.
- **Footers** (optional): e.g. `BREAKING CHANGE:`, `Refs: #123` — not for co-authors unless the user asks.

## Types

| Type | Use for |
|------|---------|
| `feat` | New user-facing behavior |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `build` | Dependencies, build tooling |
| `chore` | Maintenance (configs, cursor rules) |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `refactor` | Code change without feat/fix |
| `test` | Tests |
| `ci` | CI config |

Use scopes when helpful: `feat(home):`, `feat(app):`, `build(deps):`.

## Grouping

Prefer **several focused commits** over one large commit (deps → app wiring → views → routes/controllers → docs).

## Co-authored-by

**Never** add this line (or any Cursor agent co-author trailer) unless the user explicitly requests it:

```
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```

## Examples

```
build(deps): add ejs and @types/ejs

feat(home): serve home page via mvc controller

docs: add AGENTS.md project guide
```
